---
description: Repo-wide policy that applies regardless of which file is open
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- BookShelf is a 5-day course project. Prefer the smallest change that satisfies the
  current day's brief over a general solution for a problem we don't have yet.
- Don't add npm dependencies without asking — no router, no ORM, no test framework
  besides `node:test`, no icon library (inline SVG only).
- Don't add a real database. JSON files in `/data` are a deliberate constraint.
- Don't edit `data/*.json` by hand — go through the API so IDs and timestamps stay
  consistent.
- `packages/shared/**`: every exported type is `z.infer<typeof someSchema>` — never
  hand-write an interface that duplicates a schema. A change here touches both apps.
- Don't `console.log` outside `requestLogger`/`errorHandler` (API) or ad hoc in
  components (frontend).
- Don't widen scope. If a task lists N endpoints/components, build N — flag anything
  else you think is missing instead of adding it unasked.
